  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale up the lifesaving integrated humanitarian response in Kiremu district of East Wellega in Western Oromia, Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtIn light of the severe conflict in the East Wellega zone, Oromia regional states and the observed high needs for multi-sectoral responses by the people in the area, this project aims to scale up the humanitarian response at hotspot priority two locations in East Wellega zone of Oromia region. Moreover, this project will address the humanitarian needs of ltbgt108,511&#xa0;(32,635&#xa0;women, 21,872 girls, 31,670&#xa0;men and 22,354&#xa0;boys)&#xa0;lt/bgtIDP, Host community and returnees found in Kiremu district&#xa0;of East Wellega zone through multi-sectoral emergency response support of Health, Nutrition, Agriculture, Shelter/NFI and WASH services mainstreaming Protection activities across the sectors. WVE will utilize multi-sectoral approach, in coordination with the local partner Gurmuu Development Association, Local community, government offices and other humanitarian actors.&#xa0;The project will build on the lessons learnt from the EHF Standard Allocation 2023 Project and&#xa0;scale up lifesaving services through the maximizing good&#xa0;practices of existing structures, implementations to extend its programming in the newly targeted districts of&#xa0;Kiremu district&#xa0;of East Wellega zone of Oromia region. This mechanism will provide an opportunity for local partner to be part of the response interventions throughout the project period. The intervention will also provide a platform for the local community structure and government partners to take part in the implementation of the project to realize the intended objectives. This project will be implemented in collaboration with the local Partner called Gurmuu Development Association (GDA) and the local community. Localization, and capacity building as well as coordination of different partners in the implementation process will be ensured throughout the process. WVE will take the leadership role for this intervention and support the local partner on continuous basis to ensure the intended project results are realized with quality and value for money as well as used for the intended purposes.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
